Why Stage A refuses (a case may have several), all bands:

- nose not served (no 2D fitted field to start from): 56.6%
- blunt leading edge: normal Mach number below 1.5: 48.5%
- Mach below 1.2: 25.0%
- sharp section: leading-edge shock detached: 16.2%
- sharp section: reflected wave (served only once rung b3 passes): 14.7%
- blunt leading edge: the strip's subsonic region reaches the mirror plane between fins (spacing rule): 0.3%

The spacing rule on blunt-edged plates at normal Mach 1.5 and above (nose served), by thickness:

| Thickness | Cases | Refused by the spacing rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0.0 to 2.5 mm | 67 | 1.5% |
| 2.5 to 4.0 mm | 92 | 3.3% |
| 4.0 to 5.5 mm | 31 | 0.0% |
| 5.5 to max mm | 9 | 0.0% |

